- Verbatim check: `../2026-10-20-claude-o2-bridge/check_verbatim.py formal E10` → 24 verbatim
  blocks; new: `PathExists`, `classification`, `main`; nothing else.

## Data source and parameters
R004 `.worktrees/verify/studies/R004/src/e10_aligned.py` (read-only), the paper's retiling
(`sec:families`: cut moved from `(p,p)` to `(0,2p)`, three parallelograms of width `m = 2r + s`
and two caps, five disks, also for `r = 1`). R004's original `e10.py` (caps + six oblique
parallelograms with a `(p,p)` side) is not aligned, so it is used only as a second comparison.

Paper parameters `p, r, s` = R004 `p, r, s`. Confirmation: twice the area is
`2(6r² + 6rs + s²) + 3·4pm = 12r² + 2s² + 12rs + 24pr + 12ps`, the paper's appendix E10 row,
and E10(9,1,4) has 740 carbons and no path, the paper's "E10(9,1,4) = C740 is negative".

Cell data (the combinatorics depend on `k = p mod m` and `j = (p div m) mod 3`):
- cell 0, lower cap `L0..L5` (labels 0..5), sides `r, r+s, …`; the cuts at tube positions
  `0, m, 2m` meet it at `L0, L4, L2`;
- cell 1, upper cap `U0 U5 U4 U3 U2 U1` (`Uᵢ = 6+i`), sides `r+s, r, …`; for `k ∉ {0, r}` three
  auxiliary straight corners `12 + c` (cut at `cm`) are inserted, on the `r`-sides if `0 < k < r`,
  on the `(r+s)`-sides if `k > r`;
- cells 2..4, tube sector `c` from position `cm` to `(c+1)m`: lower corners
  `L(6−2c mod 6), L(5−2c), L(4−2c)`, vertical side `2p`, and the upper corners in the sector
  (`U(2i)` at position `p − im`, `U(2i+1)` at `p − r − im`, mod `3m`).
This is a hand derivation of the constructor's sorting of positions into four `k`-cases; the
mirror checks it reproduces the constructor's surface. All 12 combinations (4 `k`-cases × 3
values of `j`) occur in the grid.

## Mirror results (r, s = 1..5, p = 1..3m+1, plus E10(17,1,11), E10(31,1,7); 702 cases)
Every case: counts, degree sequence and isomorphism (`canonical_fast`) with R004
`e10_aligned.construct`, **and** isomorphism with R004's original `e10.construct`; twelve
degree-5 vertices; unit triangles = `12r²+2s²+12rs+24pr+12ps`; no off-seam identification (same
partition and edges as R004 `aligned_surface` on the same data, injective charts, glued pairs
only on boundaries). Bad cases: 0. Largest case: 4467 vertices.

Literal paths (exhaustive search) against the paper's condition
`∃ d ∈ {0, r, r+s}, p ≡ d ± 1 (mod m)`:

| r | s | p range | cases | paths | agree with condition |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 1..5 | 1..3m+1 | 110 | 62 | 110/110 |
| 3 | 1..5 | 1..3m+1 | 140 | 92 | 140/140 |
| 4 | 1..5 | 1..3m+1 | 170 | 92 | 170/170 |
| 5 | 1..5 | 1..3m+1 | 200 | 92 | 200/200 |
| 1 | 1..5 | 1..3m+1 | 80 | 74 | 77/80 |
| 1 | 7, 11 | 31, 17 | 2 | 0 | 2/2 |

`r ≥ 2` (620 cases, the paper's classification domain): **no disagreement**.
`r = 1` (outside the classification): negatives exactly (9,1,4), (15,1,4), (10,1,5), (11,1,5),
(17,1,5), (18,1,5), (31,1,7), (17,1,11) — including the paper's three (C740, C3038, C3542). The
paper's `r = 1` sufficiency (`p < m` or `p mod m ∈ {0,1,2,m−2,m−1}`) holds in every case, and on
this grid it is also necessary; the three formula disagreements are `p < m` positives
((3,1,4), (3,1,5), (4,1,5)). Not stated as a theorem (the paper proves no `r = 1` necessity).

## Statements (`ClaudeChallengeE10`)
```lean
def PathExists (p r s : ℤ) : Prop := ∃ n q, LiteralPath (e10Graph p r s) n q

theorem classification (p r s : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) (hr : 2 ≤ r) (hs : 1 ≤ s) :
    PathExists p r s ↔
      ∃ d : ℤ, (d = 0 ∨ d = r ∨ d = r + s) ∧
        ((p : ℤ) ≡ d + 1 [ZMOD 2 * r + s] ∨ (p : ℤ) ≡ d - 1 [ZMOD 2 * r + s])

theorem main (p₀ r₀ s₀ a b c : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p₀) (hr : 1 ≤ r₀) (hs : 1 ≤ s₀) :
    ∃ n₀ P : ℕ, 0 < P ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, n₀ ≤ n →
      (PathExists (p₀ + a * n) (r₀ + b * n) (s₀ + c * n) ↔
        PathExists (p₀ + a * (n + P)) (r₀ + b * (n + P)) (s₀ + c * (n + P)))
```
`classification` is the paper's `prop:closed` E10 row (domain `p, s ≥ 1, r ≥ 2`; the paper
marks the full graph iff as not formalized). `main` is Corollary 1b for E10 (domain
`p, r, s ≥ 1`, including the `r = 1` rays, where no closed condition is known).

## Doubts
- The cell combinatorics are not uniform in `p` (four `k`-cases, three `j`-values). This is
  forced for an aligned decomposition (straight lattice cuts from the lower boundary reach the
  upper boundary only at offsets `0` or `2p`, while upper corners sit at offset `p`), and is what
  the paper says ("cut-corner positions involve `p mod C`"). A proof of `main` must work per
  residue branch (`ClaudeChallenge2.main_residue`-style) or through the classification.
- `main` on `r = 1` rays cannot be obtained from `classification`; it needs the general
  aligned-face route or new `r = 1` results.
- Isomorphism with the aligned constructor uses R004's gluing engine; the additional isomorphism
  with R004's original non-aligned `e10.py` (its own transition-map gluing) is more independent.
